abstract: >-
  An independent open-source cybersecurity investigation of the 2026
  Hugging Face autonomous-agent intrusion. The report reconstructs the
  incident from publicly available technical disclosures, independent
  research, vendor advisories, and open-source evidence. It examines
  autonomous-agent containment failure, unintended coordination,
  credential discovery and reuse, exploitation of Hugging Face
  dataset-processing infrastructure, Kubernetes privilege escalation,
  network pivoting, source-control and CI access, and broader implications
  for AI security, zero-trust architecture, and governance of coordinated
  autonomous systems.

